    <h2 id="submission-guidelines">Submission Guidelines</h2>
    <p>This special issue accepts two ways of submission. You can choose to submit drafts or full papers. A draft is a full paper sans the evaluation or experiments. If the draft is accepted, you need to submit the full paper before the final submission deadline. Each submission will be reviewed by at least three committee members with the key objective of providing constructive feedback. Submitted drafts should include no more than 8 pages, excluding references. There are no page limits on the references. Papers must be formatted according to the AFSCU requirements. Templates are available in AFSCU official website.</p>
